# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
**/node_modules/
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# Private chatbot evaluator exports may contain user recipe ideas and provider usage.
/docs/chatbot-evals/
/release-drafts/

# next.js
**/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# Ignore all .env files
.env*

# But do NOT ignore .env.example
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Personal editor and agent tooling stays untracked. Shared agent instructions
# (AGENTS.md files and their one-line CLAUDE.md imports) are tracked; put
# machine-only notes in CLAUDE.local.md. AGENTS.override.md is ignored so a
# personal Codex override is never committed. Optional tooling worth sharing is
# listed in docs/agent-tooling.md.
.vscode/
.codex/
.claude/
.mcp.json
.agents/*
skills-lock.json
AGENTS.override.md
CLAUDE.local.md
/.local-chatgpt-client.json*
# Sentry Config File
.env.sentry-build-plugin
# Obsolete local copy of Next.js docs from the old `agents-md` codemod; the
# installed next package now ships docs in node_modules/next/dist/docs/.
.next-docs/
